### Appointment Booking System - end-to-end walkthrough
### Works with the IntelliJ HTTP Client or the VS Code "REST Client" extension.
### Everything goes through the API Gateway.
###
### The port follows GATEWAY_PORT in .env - 8080 by default, 18080 on a machine where
### something else (Apache/XAMPP) already owns 8080.

@host = http://localhost:18080

### Mailpit collects every e-mail the system sends. Open it in a browser to read the
### activation and password-reset links: http://localhost:8025
@mailpit = http://localhost:8025

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 1. PROVIDER registers
### Registration no longer returns a token - the account has to confirm its e-mail first.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ana@salon.rs",
  "password": "password123",
  "fullName": "Ana Petrović",
  "phone": "+381641234567",
  "role": "PROVIDER"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 2. CLIENT registers
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "marko@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "fullName": "Marko Marković",
  "phone": "+381601112233",
  "role": "CLIENT"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 3. Login before activation -> 403
### The message tells the user to look for the activation e-mail, which is different from
### the message an account disabled by an admin gets.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "marko@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 4. Read the activation mails
### Open http://localhost:8025 and copy the token out of each activation link, then paste
### the two values below. Both mails arrive within a second of registering.
###
### For a scripted run the tokens can also be pulled from Mailpit's own API:
###   GET {{mailpit}}/api/v1/search?query=to:ana@salon.rs
###   GET {{mailpit}}/api/v1/message/{id}     -> the token sits in the "Text" field
GET {{mailpit}}/api/v1/messages

@providerActivationToken = paste-the-token-from-the-provider-mail
@clientActivationToken = paste-the-token-from-the-client-mail

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 5. Activate the PROVIDER
# @name activateProvider
POST {{host}}/api/auth/activate?token={{providerActivationToken}}

> {% client.global.set("providerToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 6. Activate the CLIENT
# @name activateClient
POST {{host}}/api/auth/activate?token={{clientActivationToken}}

> {% client.global.set("clientToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 7. The same token works twice? -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/auth/activate?token={{clientActivationToken}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 8. Log in (now that the account is active)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "marko@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 9. Current profile
GET {{host}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{clientToken}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 10. Provider creates a service
# @name createService
POST {{host}}/api/services
Authorization: Bearer {{providerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Šišanje",
  "description": "Muško šišanje sa pranjem kose",
  "durationMinutes": 30,
  "price": 1500.00
}

> {% client.global.set("serviceId", response.body.id); %}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 11. Bulk-generate slots
### Re-running this does not duplicate slots - generation is idempotent.
POST {{host}}/api/services/{{serviceId}}/slots/generate
Authorization: Bearer {{providerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromDate": "2026-12-01",
  "toDate": "2026-12-05",
  "workDayStart": "09:00:00",
  "workDayEnd": "17:00:00",
  "skipWeekend": true,
  "zoneId": "Europe/Belgrade"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 12. Browse the catalog (no token)
GET {{host}}/api/services

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 13. Free slots for the service
# @name freeSlots
GET {{host}}/api/slots?serviceId={{serviceId}}&status=AVAILABLE

> {% client.global.set("slotId", response.body[0].id); %}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 14. Is the slot still free?
GET {{host}}/api/reservations/availability?slotId={{slotId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{clientToken}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 15. Book it
### Both the client and the provider receive a confirmation e-mail - check Mailpit.
# @name book
POST {{host}}/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{clientToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "slotId": "{{slotId}}",
  "note": "Prvi put dolazim"
}

> {% client.global.set("reservationId", response.body.id); %}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 16. Booking the same slot again -> 409
POST {{host}}/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{clientToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "slotId": "{{slotId}}"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 17. My reservations
GET {{host}}/api/reservations/my
Authorization: Bearer {{clientToken}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 18. Provider's schedule
GET {{host}}/api/reservations/provider
Authorization: Bearer {{providerToken}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 19. Cancel -> slot goes back to AVAILABLE
POST {{host}}/api/reservations/{{reservationId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{clientToken}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 20. Confirm the slot was released
GET {{host}}/api/slots/{{slotId}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 21. Forgot the password
### Always 202, even for an e-mail that is not registered - otherwise this endpoint would
### reveal which addresses exist.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/password-reset-request
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "marko@example.com"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 22. Set a new password
### The token comes from the reset mail in Mailpit and is valid for one hour, once.
@resetToken = paste-the-token-from-the-reset-mail

POST {{host}}/api/auth/password-reset
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{resetToken}}",
  "newPassword": "newPassword456"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 23. Log in with the new password
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "marko@example.com",
  "password": "newPassword456"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 24. Internal API is blocked at the gateway -> 404
GET {{host}}/api/internal/slots/{{slotId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{clientToken}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 25. No token -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/reservations/my
